{
  "_comment": [
    "The timed service definition and the machine's time policy keys.",
    "",
    "Identity is LocalService plus one privilege. timed is the only process",
    "on the machine permitted to set the clock, and SeSystemtimePrivilege is",
    "the whole of what it needs -- KACS maps it to CAP_SYS_TIME, which is",
    "what adjtimex(2) checks. It is granted to timed's *service SID* in",
    "timed-policy.reg rather than to LocalService, so trustd, resolvd and",
    "every other LocalService daemon are unaffected.",
    "",
    "RequiredPrivileges names two, and the second is not decoration:",
    "peinit REMOVES every privilege outside this list, and without",
    "SeChangeNotifyPrivilege a process cannot traverse a directory to reach",
    "a file. Naming only SeSystemtimePrivilege would produce a daemon that",
    "can set the clock and cannot open its own drift file.",
    "",
    "ExecStartPre runs prepare-state as SYSTEM (HookIdentity) to create",
    "/var/state/timed and hand it to timed's service SID. peinit provisions",
    "/run/<service> and nothing else, so a least-privileged service has no",
    "way to make itself a directory under /var/state. The alternative --",
    "running timed as SYSTEM -- would give a daemon that parses hostile",
    "network input the run of the machine. (PEI-572 would replace the hook",
    "with a StateDirectories field; the hook is what exists today.)",
    "",
    "Wants trustd and resolvd, not Requires. NTS-KE is a TLS connection,",
    "so timed needs the machine's root store and a resolver before it can",
    "authenticate a single source -- but it retries both, with backoff,",
    "for as long as it runs. A hard Requires turns a sibling's *transient*",
    "failure into timed's permanent one: on a cold boot resolvd's first",
    "launch can lose a race with authd's socket and succeed on the retry,",
    "and a machine whose clock was never set because of that would be a",
    "very confusing thing to debug. Wants gives the ordering, which is all",
    "that was wanted, without the coupling.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0): timed notifies once its socket is listening,",
    "not once the clock is right. Those are different events and only the",
    "first is a startup condition -- a service that waited for the second",
    "would hang for the length of a poll on every boot. 'The clock is",
    "trustworthy' is a question for `clock status`, and will be a readiness",
    "level of its own when PEI-500 lands.",
    "",
    "RestartPolicy is Always (2). A machine whose clock is drifting free is",
    "one whose certificates, Kerberos tickets and logs are all quietly",
    "going wrong.",
    "",
    "The Time key is created here with its defaults explicit, so that the",
    "two that matter are visible to anyone reading the registry rather than",
    "being invisible compiled-in behaviour:",
    "  AllowUnauthenticated = 0  NTS required; a network that blocks 4460",
    "                            gets an unsynchronised machine, which is",
    "                            honest, rather than one synchronised to",
    "                            whoever answered on port 123.",
    "  UseFromDHCP = 0           DHCP option 42 ignored, as on Windows. On a",
    "                            network you do not control, the DHCP",
    "                            server's idea of the time is the",
    "                            attacker's idea of the time.",
    "",
    "Servers is deliberately absent. Empty means the compiled fallback set",
    "behind 0..3.time.peios.org -- three independent operators in three",
    "jurisdictions, which is the minimum at which one liar is outvoted.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the timed package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\timed",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath", "type": "sz", "data": "/usr/sbin/timed" },
        { "name": "Triggers", "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "Identity", "type": "sz", "data": "LocalService" },
        {
          "name": "RequiredPrivileges",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": ["SeSystemtimePrivilege", "SeChangeNotifyPrivilege"]
        },
        {
          "name": "ExecStartPre",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": ["/usr/libexec/timed/prepare-state"]
        },
        { "name": "HookIdentity", "type": "sz", "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Wants", "type": "multi", "data": ["trustd", "resolvd"] },
        { "name": "Readiness", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RuntimeDirectories", "type": "multi", "data": ["timed"] },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 2 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName", "type": "sz", "data": "Time client" },
        {
          "name": "Description",
          "type": "sz",
          "data": "Keeps the system clock synchronised with authenticated network time sources"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Time",
      "values": [
        { "name": "AllowUnauthenticated", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "UseFromDHCP", "type": "dword", "data": 0 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
